{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto p-4 md:p-6 w-full font-mono">

  <!-- Header Card / Window Frame -->
  <div class="retro-card p-0 mb-6">
    <div class="window-header flex items-center justify-between p-2">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="font-bold">PRIVACY.TXT — Privacy Policy</span>
      </div>
      <a href="/" class="pixel-btn pixel-btn--sm text-xs py-0.5 px-2 text-white">
        [ &lt; Back ]
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 md:p-6 text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6">

      <!-- Effective Date Bar -->
      <div class="bg-black border border-main p-3 text-prompt flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs">
        <div><strong>VERSION:</strong> 2026.2</div>
        <div><strong>EFFECTIVE DATE:</strong> November 13, 2026</div>
        <div><strong>SERVICE URL:</strong> https://neogram.club</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 1: Overview & Philosophy -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          1. Privacy Philosophy &amp; Overview
        </h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Neogram</strong> ("we", "us", or "our") is run by Tim Wasson at <a href="https://neogram.club" class="text-mac underline">https://neogram.club</a>. We try to collect as little as possible: enough to sign you in, run chat and notifications, and publish your photos to your own website. This page explains what we store, where, and for how long.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: STRICT Mobile & SMS Privacy Policy (Carrier Mandate) -->
      <section class="space-y-3 bg-black border-2 border-prompt p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-prompt font-bold text-sm">
          <h3>2. Mobile Information &amp; SMS Privacy Policy</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="text-white font-bold">
          The following terms apply to all mobile phone numbers and SMS consent data collected by Neogram:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-black border border-prompt p-3 text-prompt space-y-2 text-xs">
          <p class="font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">
            <strong>STRICT NON-DISCLOSURE CLAUSE:</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>No mobile information will be shared with third parties/affiliates for marketing/promotional purposes. All the above categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 pl-2">
          <p>
            <strong>2.1 Purpose of Mobile Phone Collection:</strong> Mobile phone numbers you enter at sign-in are used only to send you the one-time sign-in codes you request, and to identify your account.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>2.2 No Marketing or Reselling:</strong> We do not sell, rent, lease, license, or disclose phone numbers or text messaging opt-in consent to any marketing agencies, data brokers, advertising networks, or third-party affiliates under any circumstances.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>2.3 Infrastructure Subprocessors:</strong> Phone numbers are sent over an encrypted connection to our SMS provider, Twilio Inc., only to deliver the sign-in text you requested.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Information We Collect -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          3. What we store on our server
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2 text-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-white">Account:</strong> your email address or mobile number (to sign you in), your handle, Neogram number, avatar link, status message and short bio. We don't use passwords. Sign-in codes are stored only as a one-way hash and expire after 10 minutes.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Connected websites:</strong> your site's address, folder and settings, and the API key or token you give us, stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM). We use it only to publish to and read from your site.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Social activity:</strong> who you've added as a friend, your in-app notifications, your notification settings, and a record of which photos you've liked (for visitors who aren't signed in, a one-way hash of their IP address instead of the address itself, so a photo can't be liked twice from one connection).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Guestbooks and hit counters:</strong> guestbook signatures are saved to the site owner's own website and a copy is kept in our database; hit counters store a running total per site.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Push notifications:</strong> if you turn on device notifications, the push address your browser gives us (delivered through Apple, Google or Mozilla's push services).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">A working copy of your gallery:</strong> to build your site we keep the text files of your gallery (captions, comment lists, feed files) on our server. Your photos themselves are not kept: see section 4.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Short-lived technical data:</strong> IP addresses are held in memory for rate limiting and visitor counting and are not written to our database; standard server logs are kept for troubleshooting.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Photos -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          4. Your photos live on your website
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted">
          You can only post photos once you've connected your own website (Neocities, Nekoweb or GitHub Pages). When you post, our server resizes the photo, uploads it to your site, and then deletes its copy. If the upload to your site fails, we keep the files only until the next successful publish so nothing is lost. Profile avatars work the same way. Retro filters are applied in the browser and don't change your original.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">
          Because your photos, comments and guestbook live on your own website, deleting files there deletes them for everyone; we don't keep a backup copy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Chat -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          5. Chat (NIM)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Chat messages pass through our server in memory and are not saved to our database. If the person you're messaging is offline, the message waits in our database for up to 24 hours and is deleted as soon as it's delivered (or when it expires). We record that you have a new message (who it's from, not what it says) so we can notify you. Your chat history is kept only in your own browser or the Neogram extension, and you can clear it any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Cookies & Tracking -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          6. Cookies
        </h2>
        <p>
          We use two first-party cookies: <code>neogram_session</code> keeps you signed in, and <code>neogram_active_site</code> remembers which of your websites you're working on. Your browser also stores your chat history and a few preferences locally. We don't use advertising cookies, analytics trackers or cross-site tracking.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7: Service providers -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          7. Service providers we use
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 pl-2 text-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-white">DigitalOcean</strong> hosts our server and database.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Resend</strong> delivers sign-in codes by email.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Twilio</strong> delivers sign-in codes by text message.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Apple, Google and Mozilla push services</strong> deliver device notifications, if you turn them on.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Your website host</strong> (Neocities, Nekoweb or GitHub) receives what you publish, under their own policies.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted">We don't sell or rent personal information to anyone.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8: Your choices -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          8. Download or delete your data
        </h2>
        <p>
          In <strong>Settings → Your data</strong> you can download a copy of your data as JSON or delete your account. Deleting your account removes your profile, connected-site settings and keys, friends, notifications, hit counters and guestbook copies from our server right away. Files already published to your own website stay there until you remove them. You can also email us to ask what we hold about you or to have anything corrected or removed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 9: Contact -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          9. Contact
        </h2>
        <div class="bg-black border border-main p-3 text-xs space-y-1">
          <div><strong>OPERATOR:</strong> Tim Wasson</div>
          <div><strong>EMAIL:</strong> <a href="mailto:auth@neogram.club" class="text-prompt underline">auth@neogram.club</a></div>
          <div><strong>WEBSITE:</strong> <a href="https://neogram.club" class="text-mac underline">https://neogram.club</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer Quick Links -->
      <div class="pt-4 border-t border-main flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-muted flex-wrap gap-2">
        <div>&copy; 2026 Neogram. All rights reserved.</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <a href="/terms" class="text-mac underline hover:text-white">Terms of Service &gt;&gt;</a>
          <a href="/login" class="text-prompt underline hover:text-white">Sign in &gt;&gt;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</div>
{% endblock %}
